  {
   "approach": "Launch a canoe at String Lake, carry it over the short portage to Leigh Lake, and paddle across to the lake's far western corner, where Leigh Canyon opens out and campsite 14b sits. The overland route around the lakes is long, brushy and not maintained, which is why most parties paddle. A faint climbers' path starts on the north side of the campsite and runs up Leigh Canyon, with cairns that split into several paths across the talus. The slabs lie below the large south face of No Escape Buttress, the first chunk of rock on the north side of Leigh Canyon. The easiest way to reach them is around from the west, though ledges allow a circuitous fourth class approach from the east.",
